f 17592186045417] [17592186339054 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339054 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a9/a93150906c0681b8654370267fb918076338fa8ab5bf68f50a0062a4ab34af1d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339054 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b201471a-0c40-5010-8df2-c681645f2579" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339054 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ Applying the above formula with $x=-1$ and $h=2$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{f(-1)-f(-1-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(-1)-f(-3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-(-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339056 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339056 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72075" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339056 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339056 #edb/ref 1071 "An oil tank is leaking. The volume of oil in the tank, in liters, after $t$ hours is given by the function $q(t).$ The values of $q(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $q(t)$ | $200$ | $192$ | $186$ | $182$ | $180$ |\n\nApproximate the rate at which the volume of oil in the tank is changing when $t=2$ using a backward difference approximation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339056 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de00370a-95a3-557d-bc46-f1d4bc108705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339056 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{q}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{q(t)-q(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{q(2)-q(2-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{q(2)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =186-192 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the rate of change of the volume is $-6$ liters per hour." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352532 #edb/ref 1080 "100\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352532 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352532 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6d9dee40-eb74-576e-92c5-76c16cb64c80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353510 #edb/ref 1080 "900\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353510 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353510 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dfa3e1a7-2a85-5828-93dd-859c684add2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353546 #edb/ref 1080 "800\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353546 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353546 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e349ed78-175a-5ce2-a1ed-1e87a2ab1ad3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353639 #edb/ref 1080 "200\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353639 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353639 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "edb061a8-04c3-5e4b-b27e-be6779beea3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353741 #edb/ref 1080 "600\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353741 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353741 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f918e849-9416-5f20-87b4-5595578edb5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353977 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186352532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353977 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353977 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353977 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353977 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353977 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #